# =============================================================================
# Dynamic API Validator — root .gitignore                              (OBJ-024)
#
# This repository is rooted at the existing workspace. Nothing was moved to
# create it, so every path referenced by the harness scripts, the .claude/rules
# globs and both Windows scheduled tasks still resolves exactly as before.
#
# Nested .gitignore files remain in force and are NOT duplicated wholesale here:
#   BLAST/.gitignore  ·  tools/jira/.gitignore  ·  tools/dashboard/.gitignore
#   tools/dashboard-performance/.gitignore
# The credential rules below are deliberately repeated as belt-and-braces.
# =============================================================================

# --- The two repositories that already have their own GitLab remotes ---------
# Excluded so their history and 36.19 GB of content are never duplicated here.
# Both stay fully intact on disk and keep working against their own origins;
# git simply never traverses them. Do NOT remove these two lines.
#   pam/                     -> repo.arconnet.com/root/pam.git (35.8.29_Hotfix)
#   pam_automation_bootstrap -> Omkar.Kumbhar/pam_automation_bootstrap.git (Dev)
#
# NOTE: 'Automation gitlab repo/graphify-out.local-backup-OBJ007/' (150 MB,
# 1,092 files) sits inside the excluded folder but belongs to NO git repo. It is
# captured in the verified safety snapshot, so it is not at risk — but it stays
# unversioned until its handling is decided separately.
/pam/
/Automation gitlab repo/

# --- Credentials — never commit ----------------------------------------------
# Git history cannot be un-published. Everything here must be excluded BEFORE
# the first 'git add', not corrected afterwards.
**/.env
**/*.env
!**/.env.sample
!**/*.env.sample

# Live PAM API bearer/refresh tokens written by token_guard.py.
# OBJ-025: matched by '**/' rather than a literal directory, so they stay ignored
# wherever the harness lands. A literal path here would silently stop ignoring a
# live bearer token the moment the scripts moved.
# These must stay in place on disk (an execution resume needs them) while being
# permanently disqualified from version control.
**/.token
**/.token_cache.json
**/.token_attempt_block.json

# Key material
*.pem
*.pfx
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*

# --- Regenerable build output ------------------------------------------------
# Measured at 107.57 MB / 10,145 files. Two byte-identical node_modules trees
# account for 105 MB of that on their own.
node_modules/
dist/
build/
.vite/
target/
coverage/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
*.local

# --- engage per-invocation state (OBJ-026) -----------------------------------
# Deliberately ignored, unlike .daily/ .weekly/ .drift/ .perf/ below. Those record that an
# UNATTENDED job ran and are the only evidence it did. `engage` is run by hand, often several
# times a day, and rewrites all three files each time from state that is 10 seconds old and
# fully regenerable - so tracking them would put churn in every commit and record nothing that
# the repositories themselves do not already say.
**/.engage/

# --- Scratch and transient ---------------------------------------------------
.tmp/
*.tmp
*.bak

# --- OS / editor -------------------------------------------------------------
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
~$*
*.swp
*.orig
*.rej

# =============================================================================
# Deliberately NOT ignored — recorded so a later edit does not remove them
# by mistake:
#
#   artifacts/runs/**            Measured evidence. Generated but NOT reproducible
#                              — each run is hours against a shared account, and
#                              root CLAUDE.md states runs are retained, never
#                              deleted. Includes the paused OBJ-023 run, whose
#                              checkpoint.json is its only resume state.
#   state/drift/**        facts.json, waivers.json and register.json are
#   state/weekly/**       hand-authored, and OBJ-023-RESUME.md /
#   state/perf/**         OBJ-019-STATE.md are the only record of how to
#   state/daily/**        resume paused work. *.log files here total 69 KB
#                              and are the audit trail.
#   data/sources/*.pdf    Source documents (via Git-LFS, see
#                              .gitattributes).
#   data/analysis/*.json       Root CLAUDE.md: the JSON is the source of truth
#                              and only the builder scripts write the .xlsx.
#   *.xlsx / *.pptx            Deliverables. Marked binary in .gitattributes so
#                              they never produce diff noise.
# =============================================================================

# =============================================================================
#  GitHub first push (2026-09-25) - additions
# =============================================================================
# Workbook that embeds a customer login pasted into a ticket. The capture it is
# built from was redacted before the first commit; rebuild it before re-tracking.
artifacts/workbooks/PAM-Client-Ticket-Analysis.xlsx
# More credential file types, at repo level so every clone is covered.
**/.env.*
!**/.env.sample
!**/.env.example
**/.mcp.json
**/.claude/settings.local.json
*.key
*.ppk
.git-credentials
.netrc
_netrc

# --- Local-only -------------------------------------------------------------
# The owner's private Marathi companion to CLI sessions. Never published.
mar.md
# Per-machine virtualenv (CLAUDE.md §Setup).
.venv/
